  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4605.10 Action on Compliance Certifications",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4605.10 Action on Compliance Certifications.\n\n(a) The department shall direct the regional organization to deduct CO2 allowances from, or transfer CO2 allowances to, a source’s compliance account based on the information submitted by the source, or by a CO2 AAR on behalf of the source, in compliance certifications or any other submissions required under this chapter.\n\n(b) The regional organization shall review and conduct independent audits concerning any compliance certification or any other submission under the CO2 budget trading program, and report the results of the audit to the department.\n\n(c) If the department determines that the information in the compliance certifications or other submissions under this chapter are not accurate, the department shall direct the regional organization to make the necessary adjustments to the information.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14; ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
